CP 5.6 / finding F1 — STEP 2: integration-path bisection
=========================================================
Engine under test: libcipher_rt.so.pre_cp5_3_step2  (c2c5d313, F1-broken build)
Harness: f1_step2_bisect.cpp  (extends Step 1; Mistral-7B L0 q_proj [4096,4096], M=1)
degenerate gate: nan|inf | cos<0.85 | rel>0.35   (correct = rel~0.140 cos~0.9905)

Variant A  100 sequential dispatches, NULL stream, synced between each
    iter 0   nan=0 inf=0 max_abs=0.3486 rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    iter 99  nan=0 inf=0 max_abs=0.3486 rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    RESULT A: PASS

Variant B  100 sequential dispatches, NULL stream, NO sync between (sync at end)
    final    nan=0 inf=0 max_abs=0.3486 rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    RESULT B: PASS

Variant C  100 dispatches, each wrapped in explicit cuCtxPushCurrent/Pop(primary)
    iter 0   nan=0 inf=0 max_abs=0.3486 rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    iter 99  nan=0 inf=0 max_abs=0.3486 rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    RESULT C: PASS

Variant D  100 dispatches under CUDA_INJECTION64_PATH=<c2c5d313>  (CUPTI active)
    iter 0   nan=0 inf=0 max_abs=0.3486 rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    iter 99  nan=0 inf=0 max_abs=0.3486 rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    RESULT D: PASS
    *** DIAG-T4.2.4d: total_launches=103  ctx_swaps_to_green=0
    ***               on_primary=0 on_null_stream=103
    *** => CUPTI was subscribed and saw all 103 launches, but the per-launch
    ***    green-enforcement (cipher_cupti.c:123) NEVER fired. The engine's
    ***    PrimaryCtxGuard sets cipher_rt_in_marlin_quant=1 for the whole
    ***    dispatch, which is exactly the condition that gates out the green
    ***    swap. The GEMM stays pinned to the primary context by design.

Variant E  dispatches interleaved across TWO streams, no sync between
    stream1 final  nan=0 inf=0 max_abs=0.3486 rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    stream2 final  nan=0 inf=0 max_abs=0.3486 rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    RESULT E: PASS

=========================================================
STEP 2 VERDICT: A,B,C,D,E ALL PASS — no single-context / stream-level trigger
reproduces the degeneracy. The bug is structurally unreachable by A-E.

Root mechanism (confirmed in cipher_rt_marlin_engine.cpp PrimaryCtxGuard +
cipher_rt_marlin_engine_dispatch, and by Variant D's ctx_swaps_to_green=0):

  c2c5d313's cipher_rt_marlin_engine_dispatch UNCONDITIONALLY wraps the GEMM
  launch in PrimaryCtxGuard, which:
    (a) cuCtxSetCurrent(primary)  -> GEMM + its write to output buffer C run
        on the PRIMARY context, regardless of the caller's context;
    (b) cipher_rt_in_marlin_quant=1 -> CUPTI's per-launch green-enforcement
        is suppressed for the GEMM (proven: D's ctx_swaps_to_green=0).

  A-E all run in ONE context (the harness's primary). GEMM producer and
  consumer share that context => coherent => correct output every time.

  The real decode breaks because the host app runs its surrounding decode
  kernels on a GREEN CUcontext (the 8-SM partition CUPTI green-enforcement
  switches app threads onto). c2c5d313 pins the GEMM + buffer-C write to the
  PRIMARY context. Producer (primary) and consumer (green) are on DIFFERENT
  contexts with independent, unsynchronized streams => the green-context
  consumer races the primary-context GEMM => garbage logits => argmax(0).

  This is also why CP 5.3 STEP 2's dc804eb3 fix works: it skips the
  PrimaryCtxGuard when a green context is active (engine.cpp:1005-1011), so
  the GEMM launches on the caller's green context/stream — same context as
  the consumer => ordered => coherent.

MINIMAL TRIGGER: cross-CONTEXT, not cross-stream. Requires a second (green)
CUcontext with the GEMM-output consumer on it. A-E cannot express this.
Next step = Variant F: real green/secondary context, consumer kernel reads C
with no cross-context sync — expected to reproduce the degeneracy.
